      "claim": "The intermediate range of the short‑run aggregate supply (SRAS) curve is upward sloping.",
      "evidence": "Macroeconomic textbooks divide SRAS into three segments: Keynesian (horizontal), intermediate (upward‑sloping), and classical (vertical). The intermediate segment reflects that some resources are idle, so firms can increase output at a rising marginal cost.",
